(2298781, 314431, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kenskid:</b></div><hr/><i> Always near the top Bear...good job. Can''t we do something about the 1,2,and 3 votes on great shots like this!?!?!? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanx for the kind words. Check my "yellow" and "refractions" when they finish to see I''m most assuredly NOT always near the top :-)<br/> <br/>As for the low votes, I don''t see enough of them on this shot to bother me. Some people just don''t like hyper-processing, which this most asuredly is. The colors have been goosed and manipulated to suit my vision of what the scene looked like, and they are what I call "hyper-real"; ditto the aggressive sharpening. It''s not to everyone''s taste.</td>', 'Originally posted by kenskid: Always near the top Bear...good job. Can''t we do something about the 1,2,and 3 votes on great shots like this!?!?!?   Thanx for the kind words. Check my "yellow" and "refractions" when they finish to see I''m most assuredly NOT always near the top :-) As for the low votes, I don''t see enough of them on this shot to bother me. Some people just don''t like hyper-processing, which this most asuredly is. The colors have been goosed and manipulated to suit my vision of what the scene looked like, and they are what I call "hyper-real"; ditto the aggressive sharpening. It''s not to everyone''s taste.', '2006-04-09 01:56:48.000000', NULL, 0),
