(2299245, 314578, 332, '<td valign="top">Rámaði mjög innilega í að hafa séð þessa einhvers staðar áður. Þannig að hún hlaut að vera íslensk. Var hún ekki í einhverri keppni á ljosmyndari.is eða í mbl.is ljósmyndakeppninni eða eitthvað svoleiðis?</td>', 'Rámaði mjög innilega í að hafa séð þessa einhvers staðar áður. Þannig að hún hlaut að vera íslensk. Var hún ekki í einhverri keppni á ljosmyndari.is eða í mbl.is ljósmyndakeppninni eða eitthvað svoleiðis?', '2006-04-09 12:07:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2299249, 314480, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by yanko:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ltsimring:</b></div><hr/><i> nice image, Rikki, but what about "adding a major element" clause?! It''s got to be pretty major if the title is "Rays of Light"... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>There were special Advance Editing rules in this one which basically said there were no rules except you couldn''t splice multiple images together. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Oops, my bad! I did not take part in this challenge (did not have any original files from 2002), so did not pay close attention to the rules. Congrats on the fine image and the well deserved high score then! :)</td>', 'Originally posted by yanko: Originally posted by ltsimring: nice image, Rikki, but what about "adding a major element" clause?! It''s got to be pretty major if the title is "Rays of Light"...   There were special Advance Editing rules in this one which basically said there were no rules except you couldn''t splice multiple images together.   Oops, my bad! I did not take part in this challenge (did not have any original files from 2002), so did not pay close attention to the rules. Congrats on the fine image and the well deserved high score then! :)', '2006-04-09 12:08:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2299251, 314935, 10985, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RKT:</b></div><hr/><i> This was so cool Louison...it has such a nice old school vibe about it...I really like the toning too...it makes me think of summer for some reason...perhaps it is the carefree attitude he seems to have...speaking of warmer weather...Have any daffodil or crocus popped through the earth up there yet? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>In the southern-most parts of the province, yes. Muscari, tulips, crocuses, etc. In Québec city, I haven''t seen any yet.<br/> <br/>Thanks Rachel.</td>', 'Originally posted by RKT: This was so cool Louison...it has such a nice old school vibe about it...I really like the toning too...it makes me think of summer for some reason...perhaps it is the carefree attitude he seems to have...speaking of warmer weather...Have any daffodil or crocus popped through the earth up there yet?   In the southern-most parts of the province, yes. Muscari, tulips, crocuses, etc. In Québec city, I haven''t seen any yet. Thanks Rachel.', '2006-04-09 12:13:00.000000', NULL, 0),
